.TH MOCHI-PURGE-DATA 1 "2026-09-28" "Mochi @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mochi-purge-data \- explicitly remove the current user's Mochi data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mochi-purge-data
.RB [ --purge ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without --purge, removes nothing. Stop Mochi before invoking this command.
Normal package removal and reinstallation preserve user data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --purge
Permanently remove this user's Mochi configuration, resources and state.
Release signing identities are preserved in both
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mochi-release-signing and the legacy
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mochi/release-signing directory, including its public identity
files. XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config. Purge does not migrate keys.
Run as the owning user, never with sudo.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mochi-manager (1)
